    "q-132285": {
      "dom_id": "step-q132285",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}({x}^{2}+2y)\\,dy\\,dx=$",
      "worked_solution": "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}({x}^{2}+2y)\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}({x}^{2}+2y)\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}]_{{x}^{2}}^{1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+1-{x}^{4}-{x}^{4})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+1-2{x}^{4})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+1-2{x}^{4})\\,dx & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x-\\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+1-\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
